#
# Claim under probe (pi-runtime-contract.md §10 F-BUSY-NUDGE, status UNPROVEN):
#   a turn_end boundary handler returning { entries: [{ type: "custom_message", ... }],
#   continue: true } makes pi (a) append the custom_message to the session, (b) run ONE
#   more model request IN THE SAME RUN with the custom message in LLM context (role=user),
#   WITHOUT an intervening agent_settled. This is the §7 B1 delivery path for the
#   read-streak self-nudge to a BUSY agent.
#
# Shape (6 turns; the probe hook in r10-1-busy-nudge-probe.test.mjs injects):
#   t1: text + native read toolcall, stopReason toolUse (run keeps looping naturally)
#   t2: text + native read toolcall, stopReason toolUse -> MID marker injected at this turn_end;
#       the marker request follows a read toolResult within the same run (P1 evidence)
#   t3: text + native read toolcall, stopReason toolUse — consumed by the MID continuation
#   t4: text only, stopReason stop -> run would normally END here; STOP marker injected at
#       this turn_end proves continue:true creates a request that would NOT otherwise exist (P2)
#   t5: text only, stopReason stop — consumed by the STOP continuation request
#   t6: text only, stopReason stop — terminal settle of the probe lane
# Control lane (same fixture, hook injects nothing) consumes exactly t1..t4.
